Package: rts2-viewer
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Remote Telescope System 2 - Qt camera viewer client
 RTS2 (Remote Telescope System, 2nd version) is a distributed control
 system for robotic astronomical observatories.
 .
 This package contains rts2-viewer: a Qt5 GUI client that connects to a
 running camera device over the RTS2 wire protocol, displays incoming
 images with a logfit display stretch, and provides a draggable measure
 cursor with live centroid/FWHM fitting and a focus-progress graph. It
 is a standalone network client - point it at any centrald with
 --server/--device, whether local or remote - and does not require
 rts2-base to be installed on the same machine.

Package: rts2-stacker
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Remote Telescope System 2 - Qt camera stacking demonstrator
 RTS2 (Remote Telescope System, 2nd version) is a distributed control
 system for robotic astronomical observatories.
 .
 This package contains rts2-stacker: a clone of rts2-viewer that shows
 how a CCD image builds up. Every frame received from the camera is
 dark-subtracted and flat-fielded with master calibration frames from a
 directory given on the command line (--calib), added into a running
 sum displayed live, and the sum is saved as a FITS file on reset.
 Exposure times are limited to those with a master dark. No image
 registration is done - the telescope's guider is relied upon.
